{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792774535,"nonce":"hJgWnJLpikYIb8JFuHXqioVwdJ8=","message":"**Typed census, reproduced in ashui alone (2026-10-23)**\n\nScratch program: 1,000 elements of each kind in one tree, Ash's `hl.Gc.dumpMemory` after two majors and a pause, typed counts minus the empty program's, on the hybrid runtime built from ash main 58c779b7. Per element:\n\n- a bare `\u003cdiv/\u003e`: 1.3 KB of live Haxe heap. 9 String, 6 ArrayObj, 3 array\u003cdynamic\u003e, 3 array\u003cString\u003e, 2 StringBuf, 1 Identity, 1 Node, 1 Owner, 1 ArrayBytes_Int (FieldSet).\n- a `\u003cdiv class=\"row\"\u003e` that a `:hover` rule matches: 2.3 KB. Adds 8 SignalBool, 1 Interaction, 2 Brush, 1 Watch, a StringMap and its iterator, 2 more ArrayBytes_Int.\n- a `\u003ctext\u003e`: 1.5 KB (a TextNode, a Text, 2 FieldSets).\n- a row of one div and two texts: 4.7 KB.\n\nSo the Haxe heap of an element is a few KB, not the 285 KB a node that `currentMemory` reports for ChimpMonk's shell. The difference is the 4 KiB pressure charge on each finalizable handle (ash docs/debugging.md): a styled, interactive div holds about 10 handles (8 SignalBool from Interaction, a Watch, a Computed or two), which is 40 KB of charge that is not memory. It makes the collector see a heap several times too big. ChimpMonk's 4,703 Watches at about 2,650 nodes is 18 MB of charge for Watches alone.\n\n**What follows**\n\n1. Interaction makes 8 SignalBool eagerly (hovered, pressed, focused, focusVisible, focusWithin, disabled, checked, indeterminate). Most elements are read through at most one or two, and non-reactive callers (Pointer on every event, Focus, Keyboard) read `.disabled.get()` as a plain Bool. Making them lazy, with the Bool as the truth and a signal made on first reactive read, takes 6 to 7 handles out of each interactive element. Filed as its own issue.\n2. The measure-cache finding in 99b1c2a came out of this: a first layout of 900 text nodes took 70 to 90 s.\n3. 5 live StringBuf per row of three nodes is unexplained: no ashui class keeps one in a field. Left for Ash's census, which can name the holder.\n4. The `Map` that cost a hash table per node is already gone (61510d3).","files":null}]}